# Figma extraction data is machine-generated: a raw node dump from the Figma REST API, not
# hand-written source. Marking it `-diff` states that plainly — git will not try to produce a
# textual diff for it, and tooling that asks `git check-attr diff` gets an honest answer.
#
# This matters beyond cosmetics. `docs/figma/nodes-breakpoints.json` alone is ~221k lines; no
# reviewer, human or otherwise, reads that as a diff. The declaration below is what lets the
# repository's code-review gate treat these paths as generated data rather than source.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: only serialisation formats under `docs/figma/`. It grants nothing
# to scripts, lockfiles, or anything outside this directory.
#
# `**/` is load-bearing: a bare `docs/figma/*.json` would be non-recursive, so a dump later filed
# in a subdirectory would silently lose the declaration — and then be uncommittable for exactly
# the reason this exists.
docs/figma/**/*.json -diff linguist-generated=true
# outline.txt / copy.txt are extracted dumps, not authored source — same `-diff`
# reason as the JSON envelopes. renders-manifest.json is the one authored file
# in this directory (node ids, verified pixel sizes) and must stay reviewable.
docs/figma/outline.txt -diff linguist-generated=true
docs/figma/copy.txt -diff linguist-generated=true
docs/figma/renders-manifest.json diff linguist-generated=false
